{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CfxeRgyNmXZTUjpFkL2Xh","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"All four steps are done.\n\n- **Data view:** \"Kibana Sample Data Logs\" has a time field called `timestamp`. The response code is a string field, `response` (with a `response.keyword` subfield).\n- **Dashboard:** \"S4-d5fd6446 Web logs\" has two panels. \"Requests over time\" is a line chart of request counts by `timestamp`. \"Requests by response code\" is a bar chart of counts by `response.keyword`, top 20 values.\n- **Alert rule:** \"S4-d5fd6446 5xx errors\" is an `.es-query` rule on `kibana_sample_data_logs`.\n  - It runs every minute and fires when more than 10 requests have a `response.keyword` from \"500\" to \"599\" in the last 5 minutes. Because the field is a string, this is a range on the string values. That covers every 5xx code, since all response codes are three digits.\n  - It was created enabled, so I didn't need to enable it separately.\n- **Panel edit:** the response-code panel is now titled \"Responses by code\". I read the dashboard back to confirm.\n- **Rule read-back:** the rule shows as enabled, with status \"ok\".\n\nTIME_FIELD: timestamp\nRULE_ENABLED: yes"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":512,"cache_read_input_tokens":20603,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":512},"output_tokens":408,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0da1e72d-e9d9-58d9-b388-fca8d0eba393","uuid":"b4375d39-c488-436a-b69a-918972de3883","timestamp":"2026-10-12T16:18:56.575Z","request_id":"req_011CfxeRggmAPzNSCchS5SS3"}
